{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XdcN3jJtPJVWtpaC1uRXAM","type":"tool_result","content":"2:  \"$comment\": \"Shared deep-loop offer cases. Read by the TypeScript offer-gate test and the Python advisor test, so the native gate and the Python fallback agree on which prompts ask for a loop run, which complain about a stuck run and which write about the loop. asksForLoopRun is the full gate, after the past-run, stuck-run, write-about and question exceptions. typedReviewKept, where present, says whether a typed /deep:review keeps its command: attachCommand on a single review route in TypeScript, and the run row in the Python gate.\",\n118:    { \"id\": \"typed-refused\", \"prompt\": \"don't run /deep:review, explain the review loop\", \"asksForLoopRun\": false, \"stuckRun\": false, \"writingAbout\": false, \"typedReviewKept\": false },\n119:    { \"id\": \"typed-question\", \"prompt\": \"what does /deep:review do?\", \"asksForLoopRun\": false, \"stuckRun\": false, \"writingAbout\": false, \"typedReviewKept\": false },\n120:    { \"id\": \"typed-doc-path\", \"prompt\": \"see (/deep:review.md) for the flags\", \"asksForLoopRun\": false, \"stuckRun\": false, \"writingAbout\": false, \"typedReviewKept\": false },\n121:    { \"id\": \"typed-stuck\", \"prompt\": \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\", \"asksForLoopRun\": false, \"stuckRun\": true, \"writingAbout\": false, \"typedReviewKept\": false },\n122:    { \"id\": \"typed-control\", \"prompt\": \"/deep:review:confirm the auth module\", \"asksForLoopRun\": false, \"stuckRun\": false, \"writingAbout\": false, \"typedReviewKept\": true }\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/decision-record.md:63:**How it works**: the replacement check is that five of the six prompts sit in the corpus as `near-miss` rows: N7 as `nm-system-deep-loop-02`, N9 as `-03`, V7 as `-05`, H6 as `nm-sk-code-02` and A3 as `nm-sk-code-03`. D1 is now a positive `/doctor:deep-loop` row, `cmd-doctor-deep-loop-plain-tune-02`, because D10 fixed the stuck-run complaint instead of recording it as a miss. The guards that D10 added are covered by the shared fixture and the guard tests.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/decision-record.md:601:v4.2.0.0 covers the expanded deep modes themselves: expansive depth, open nodes holding the stop, --extend, fan-out and dispatch. It says nothing about today's deep-loop offer work in packet 012: the advisor offering /deep:* only on explicit loop asks, the one-question offer with the flags already filled in, setup through the question tool, and /doctor:deep-loop for stuck runs. Should I add it?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/decision-record.md:970:The fresh Opus review found real gaps in the deep-loop offer epic (I reproduced 6 of them): refusals like \"don't do deep research\" still get the offer, a typed `/deep:review:confirm` still gets an A/B/C hint recommending :auto, questions like \"how many iterations does deep research run\" get the offer, \"deep-review\" with a hyphen loses it, and \"not stuck\" still routes to the doctor. Some packet claims also overstate the evidence. What should happen?","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:46:46.629Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2:  \"$comment\": \"Shared deep-loop offer cases. Read by the TypeScript offer-gate test and the Python advisor test, so the native gate and the Python fallback agree on which prompts ask for a loop run, which complain about a stuck run and which write about the loop. asksForLoopRun is the full gate, after the past-run, stuck-run, write-about and question exceptions. typedReviewKept, where present, says whether a typed /deep:review keeps its command: attachCommand on a single review route in TypeScript, and the run row in the Python gate.\",\n118:    { 