p-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:40-57`","+- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/spec.md:194-235`","+","+## Findings by Severity","+","+### P0 Findings","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+1. **A typed /deep:review on a stuck-run complaint overrides the /doctor:deep-loop answer in the served output** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:434 -- `attachCommand` answers a stuck-run complaint with `/doctor:deep-loop` (command-attach.ts:837-841), but both return paths of the handler then pass the result through `attachTypedCommand` (advisor-recommend.ts:556, :628), which replaces the top row's command with whatever `typedCommandForTop` returns (advisor-recommend.ts:434-446). `typedCommandForTop` checks only `commandOnlyMentioned` and ownership (command-attach.ts:257-265); it never consults `isStuckRunComplaint`. Executed: for \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\", `attachCommand` returns `/deep:review`-free `/doctor:deep-loop` while `typedCommandForTop('system-deep-loop', ...)` returns `/deep:review`. The shared fixture row `typed-stuck` says `typedReviewKept: false` (deep-loop-offer-cases.json:121) and the Python gate drops the run row on that prompt, but the TypeScript test only asserts `attachCommand` (deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:57), so the end-to-end surface the reader sees carries `/deep:review` with `typed: true`, a new costly run for a reader who reported a stuck one, and the TS and Python surfaces disagree on the very case REQ-020 names.","+   Finding class: correctness","+   Scope proof: command-attach.ts and advisor-recommend.ts are in the review scope file; REQ-020 names this prompt.","+   Affected surface hints: typedCommandForTop, attachTypedCommand, deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts typed cases","+   Case: prompt \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\" with system-deep-loop as the top recommendation.","+","+```json","+{\"type\":\"correctness\",\"claim\":\"The served TS recommendation for a stuck-run complaint that also types /deep:review carries /deep:review (typed) instead of /doctor:deep-loop, contradicting the fixture's typedReviewKept=false and the Python gate.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:434\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:628\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:257\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:837\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/fixtures/deep-loop-offer-cases.json:121\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:57\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Looked for a stuck or doctor check in typedCommandForTop and attachTypedCommand, and for an ADR saying a typed command outranks the stuck diagnosis; found neither. The fixture comment defines typedReviewKept as the TS attachCommand result, which is why the suite passes.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The scorer may put command-doctor-deep-loop on top for this prompt, in which case typedCommandForTop returns undefined (owner system-deep-loop != command row id) and no override happens. Not verified end to end because runtime dist is missing in this worktree.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.75,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"An end-to-end advisor run showing the top row is the doctor command row (not system-deep-loop) for this prompt, or an ADR that ranks the typed command above the stuck diagnosis.\"}","+```","+","+### P2 Findings","+1. **Common refusal verbs still open the loop gate in both copies** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:440 -- `RUN_ASK_NEGATED` lists `do not|don't|never|no need to|need not|without|not asking for|not looking for` and a bare `no`, but not `skip`, `avoid`, `instead of`, `rather than` or \"no need for\", although `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` (command-attach.ts:686) treats `skip` and `avoid` as refusals of a typed command. Executed: \"skip the deep review, just explain\", \"avoid a deep review here\" and \"there is no need for a deep review\" each return `/deep:review` from `attachCommand` and `True` from Python `asks_for_loop_run` with the run row kept. REQ-015's six enumerated phrasings pass; these neighbours do not. Policy stays `ask`, so the cost is one unwanted question.","+   Finding class: correctness","+   Scope proof: command-attach.ts:440 and skill_advisor.py:4666 are the two gate copies under review.","+   Affected surface hints: RUN_ASK_NEGATED, _RUN_ASK_NEGATED_RE, deep-loop-offer-cases.json refusal rows","+   Case: prompt \"skip the deep review, just explain the parser bug\" on a single review route.","+","+## Traceability Checks","+- spec_code (partial): REQ-015/REQ-016/REQ-017/REQ-018/REQ-019 example prompts reproduced through `attachCommand` give the stated results (e.g. \"do a deep review of the parser\" keeps `/deep:review`, \"don't do a deep review...\" withholds). REQ-020's typed-stuck prompt agrees at the `attachCommand` level only; the served output diverges (P1 above).","+","+## Integration Evidence","+- `advisor-recommend.ts` `enrichCompiledRoutes` -> `attachTypedCommand` ordering at :556 and :628.","+- Live CLI `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` could not run: `runtime/dist/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.js` is missing in this worktree (exit 69). Rebuilding would write outside the lineage, so it was not done.","+","+## Edge Cases","+- Ambiguity: end-to-end confirmation of the P1 depends on which row tops the prompt; recorded in the adjudication packet as the downgrade trigger.","+- Python and TS agree on the refusal gap (both miss), so it is a shared-vocabulary gap rather than drift.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+- Hyphen spelling (\"deep-review\"), curly apostrophe folding, \"not stuck, run 5 more iterations\", \"how many iterations does deep research run\" all behave as REQ-016 to REQ-018 state.","+- Typed mode suffix `:auto`/`:confirm` keeps the typed command (`typedCommandIn` -> `/deep:review`).","+","+## Ruled Out","+- No-edit wording beside a typed `/deep:review` (\"/deep:review the parser, no edits\") keeps the typed command; ruled out as a defect because the reader typed the command and a deep review does not edit the reviewed code.","+","+## Next Focus","+- Dimension: security","+- Focus area: policy and trust surfaces of the offer (NFR-S01 `ask` never `run`), regex catastrophic backtracking in the gate patterns, and the Python fallback's subprocess path.","+- Reason: correctness covered the main gate; security is next in rotation.","+- Rotation status: 1 of 4 dimensions done.","+- Required evidence: policy derivation for deep rows; timing of gate regexes on long adversarial input.","+","+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-2/iterations/iteration-001.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U7KiR1KwBWTnkMqCAm7qEc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
