{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxyB3LoN8QB14rXJ338KXZ","type":"tool_result","content":"commit c8eee36a1f56ca99e29daa4de730c40d040a4626\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<email>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 23 20:24:30 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): withhold deep-loop offers on refusals and subjects\n    \n    The deep-loop gate offered /deep:research or /deep:review when a prompt\n    turned the loop down in words, asked how many passes the loop runs, named\n    the loop's own code or results, or used a count to describe a subject. It\n    also missed the hyphen spelling and a curly apostrophe, and read \"not\n    stuck\" as a stuck run. The gate now reads each loop phrase on its own and\n    skips one that a refusal leads or follows, or that names the request's\n    subject. The Python fallback carries the same rules and now reads a typed\n    command with the TypeScript boundary and mention checks.\n    \n    A typed deep-loop command now carries a typed flag through the recommend\n    output, so the brief prints plain (ask) instead of offering a mode the\n    reader already chose. The routing baseline was recaptured because one\n    refused holdout row stopped carrying a command.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers\n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/013-deep-loop-offer-in-hint\n    Commit-Id: 0015965\n\n .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.2.0.0.md             |  16 +-\n .skilled/hooks/injection-contract.md               |   2 +-\n .../hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts        |   3 +\n .../runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts          |   1 +\n .../system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md     |   2 +-\n .../runtime/lib/command-attach.ts                  | 110 +++++++++--\n .../system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts     |   4 +-\n .../system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts |   2 +\n .../runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts        |   3 +\