{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM9r7DjeVFwUEZ3JnWgU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PvfTtFc7x3yAxCVz4bLRD3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring; grep -n \"^| AC-008\" $S/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md | grep -o \"| [A-Za-z]* | [A-Z0-9-]* |$\"; grep -n \"^## ADR-\\|^### ADR-\\|^# ADR\\|ADR-00[0-9]:\" $S/012-deep-loop-command-offers/decision-record.md | head; grep -n \"typed\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts | head; sed -n 1,60p $S/013-deep-loop-offer-in-hint/spec.md | sed -n 25,60p"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8186,"cache_read_input_tokens":231228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8186},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:24.671Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PvfTtFc7x3yAxCVz4bLRD3":{"command":"S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring; grep -n \"^| AC-008\" $S/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md | grep -o \"| [A-Za-z]* | [A-Z0-9-]* |$\"; grep -n \"^## ADR-\\|^### ADR-\\|^# ADR\\|ADR-00[0-9]:\" $S/012-deep-loop-command-offers/decision-record.md | head; grep -n \"typed\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts | head; sed -n 1,60p $S/013-deep-loop-offer-in-hint/spec.md | sed -n 25,60p"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PvfTtFc7x3yAxCVz4bLRD3","type":"tool_result","content":"| Waived | ADR-003 |\n33:## ADR-001: Supersede the near-miss count in AC-019 with the operator's reversal D10\n128:## ADR-002: Keep or drop the \"multi-round research\" alias after an out-of-domain hit\n223:## ADR-003: Waive AC-008 on the measured offer rate\n317:## ADR-004: Narrow D2 so a loop name about the loop's own code is not an ask\n248:  // A typed command, with or without a mode suffix, is the reader's own choice,\n250:  return policyPart === 'ask' && DEEP_LOOP_OFFER_COMMANDS.has(commandPart) && recommendation.typed !== true\n310: * scorer knows which skills a typed command held below the top and which only cleared\n517: * Render the model-visible advisor brief from typed advisor output only.\n| **Created** | 2026-11-23 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/527-deep-loop-offer-in-hint` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe advisor brief names a deep-loop command as `system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask)` and nothing more. The three-option offer (A run it with `:auto`, B `:confirm`, C no loop) lives only in the command doc, so a session that asks for the review target first never opens that doc and never asks the offer. Packet `012-deep-loop-command-offers` measured this on prompt F6: after its routing-step edit, one of four sessions asked the full offer and the other three asked for the target first.\n\n### Purpose\nA session that sees a `/deep:research` or `/deep:review` command with policy `ask` in the brief can ask the three-option offer without opening the command doc first.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n$ printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"extend the finished deep review by 3 iterations\",\"session_id\":\"probe\",\"cwd\":\"<repo root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\\n    | node .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"additionalContext\":\"Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask) 0.95/0.12 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: NEVER embed ADR-/REQ-/CHK-/task-ids or spec paths in code comments — forbidden regardless of instruction. Write the durable WHY instead. Pre-commit gate blocks violations.\"}}\n\nRun 2026-11-23 in worktree 527 at 72599d47a52. F6 rate from packet 012 after its routing-step edit: 1 of 4 sessions asked the offer\n(scratch/behaviour/F6-after-step0.md and F6-sample-1.md to F6-sample-3.md in that packet).\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:27.333Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| Waived | ADR-003 |\n33:## ADR-001: Supersede the near-miss count in AC-019 with the operator's reversal D10\n128:## ADR-002: Keep or drop the \"multi-round research\" alias after an out-of-domain hit\n223:## ADR-003: Waive AC-008 on the measured offer rate\n317:## ADR-004: Narrow D2 so a loop name about the loop's own code is not an ask\n248:  // A typed command, with or without a mode suffix, is the reader's own choice,\n250:  return policyPart === 'ask' && DEEP_LOOP_OFFER_COMMANDS.has(commandPart) && recommendation.typed !== true\n310: * scorer knows which skills a typed command held below the top and which only cleared\n517: * Render the model-visible advisor brief from typed advisor output only.\n| **Created** | 2026-11-23 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/527-deep-loop-offer-in-hint` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe advisor brief names a deep-loop command as `system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask)` and nothing more. The three-option offer (A run it with `:auto`, B `:confirm`, C no loop) lives only in the command doc, so a session that asks for the review target first never opens that doc and never asks the offer. Packet `012-deep-loop-command-offers` measured this on prompt F6: after its routing-step edit, one of four sessions asked the full offer and the other three asked for the target first.\n\n### Purpose\nA session that sees a `/deep:research` or `/deep:review` command with policy `ask` in the brief can ask the three-option offer without opening the command doc first.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n$ printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"extend the finished deep review by 3 iterations\",\"session_id\":\"probe\",\"cwd\":\"<repo root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\\n    | node .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"additionalContext\":\"Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask) 0.95/0.12 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: NEVER embed ADR-/REQ-/CHK-/task-ids or spec paths in code comments — forbidden regardless of instruction. Write the durable WHY instead. Pre-commit gate blocks violations.\"}}\n\nRun 2026-11-23 in worktree 527 at 72599d47a52. F6 rate from packet 012 after its routing-step edit: 1 of 4 sessions asked the offer\n(scratch/behaviour/F6-after-step0.md and F6-sample-1.md to F6-sample-3.md in that packet).\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PvfTtFc7x3yAxCVz4bLRD3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM9s5FDB64DY3i68i1JJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EGsZCPNgS33dqshPnJrDEP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 225,275p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts; S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/013-deep-loop-offer-in-hint; grep -n \"REQ-0\\|Status\\b\" $S/spec.md | head -20"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2098,"cache_read_input_tokens":239414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2098},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:32.333Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EGsZCPNgS33dqshPnJrDEP":{"command":"sed -n 225,275p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts; S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/013-deep-loop-offer-in-hint; grep -n \"REQ-0\\|Status\\b\" $S/spec.md | head -20"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EGsZCPNgS33dqshPnJrDEP","type":"tool_result","content":"// fields stay authoritative and the generated row fills only what they omit, so a\n// caller that already resolved the command is never second-guessed.\nfunction commandLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  // A hub that withheld its mode must not regress to the command its generated\n  // row names, because that command is the mode the reader has not chosen yet.\n  const row = recommendation.needsMode === true ? undefined : commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n  const command = recommendation.command ?? row?.command;\n  const owner = recommendation.ownerSkillId ?? row?.ownerSkillId ?? recommendation.skill;\n  const policy = recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy;\n  const commandPart = command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n  const ownerPart = sanitizeSkillLabel(owner);\n  if (!commandPart || !ownerPart) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  // The class belongs to the command printed, not to the skill that carried it,\n  // so a recommendation that names another command takes that command's class.\n  const mutating = row !== undefined && row.command === commandPart\n    ? row.mutating\n    : Object.values(COMMAND_ROWS).find((candidate) => candidate.command === commandPart)?.mutating;\n  const policyPart = policyWord(policy, mutating, childSession);\n  if (policyPart === null) {\n    return `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart}`;\n  }\n  // A typed command, with or without a mode suffix, is the reader's own choice,\n  // so the head prints it plainly instead of offering a choice already made.\n  return policyPart === 'ask' && DEEP_LOOP_OFFER_COMMANDS.has(commandPart) && recommendation.typed !== true\n    ? `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (ask: A ${commandPart}:auto (Recommended), B ${commandPart}:confirm, C no loop)`\n    : `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (${policyPart})`;\n}\n\n// A doctor bridge renders as its runnable command and never as its raw id; an\n// unmapped doctor id renders nothing.\nfunction recommendationLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  return commandLabel(recommendation, childSession)\n    ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(recommendation.skill)\n      ? doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill)\n      : sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill));\n}\n\n// A companion is a command the reader may act on, so it carries the same policy\n// word the head carries. A child still gets the downgrade marker because that\n// command must not be started there.\nfunction companionCommandLabel(skillId: string, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  const command = doctorCommandString(skillId);\n  if (command === null) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  const row = commandRowFor(skillId);\n  const word = policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession);\n  return word === null ? command : `${command} (${word})`;\n}\n18:<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n24:| **Status** | Complete |\n94:| REQ-001 | The brief head for a `/deep:research` or `/deep:review` command with policy word `ask` names options A, B and C, with A the command plus `:auto` and B the command plus `:confirm`. | The Measured Behavior command prints `system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop)` in its first line, and the golden test for `/deep:research` expects the research names. |\n95:| REQ-002 | Every other command label renders as before. | `npx vitest run` in the advisor runtime reports 0 failed, and the golden heads for `/doctor:git hooks (ask)` and every non-deep row are unchanged in the diff. |\n96:| REQ-003 | A child session keeps the `parent-named only` label with no options. | A test renders a `/deep:review` recommendation with `childSession: true` and expects `(parent-named only)` with no `A ` option text. |\n102:| REQ-004 | The longer head still fits the default token cap with its companion line. | A test renders a `/deep:review` head with a `/doctor:deep-loop` companion at the default cap and expects both lines. |\n103:| REQ-005 | F6 is sampled four times after the change and the rate is recorded. | `implementation-summary.md` states how many of four F6 sessions asked the three-option offer, with each run's file under `scratch/behaviour/`. |\n104:| REQ-006 | A command the operator typed shows no offer options. For `/deep:review:confirm the auth module` and `/deep:research:auto vector index compaction` the brief prints `/deep:review (ask)` and `/deep:research (ask)` with no `A ` option text. | The prompt hook prints those heads, and a golden test pins each. |\n105:| REQ-007 | The tests pin the options to the deep-loop commands only. The head-length test accepts the colon form for `/deep:*` alone, and a golden test covers the offer in an ambiguous two-skill head. | Both tests fail when the options leak onto a non-deep `ask` command or drop out of the ambiguous head. |\n106:| REQ-008 | The packet says what was measured. `implementation-summary.md` states the eight-run result where it claimed sessions learn the options, quotes the final head, and records whether the Pi hand check ran. | `rg -n 'now learns' implementation-summary.md` prints nothing. |\n127:| Dependency | The behaviour arena from packet 012 (`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `claude -p` with a budget cap) | Without it SC-002 cannot be measured | Record REQ-005 as deferred with the reason and keep SC-001 as the closure evidence |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:34.797Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// fields stay authoritative and the generated row fills only what they omit, so a\n// caller that already resolved the command is never second-guessed.\nfunction commandLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  // A hub that withheld its mode must not regress to the command its generated\n  // row names, because that command is the mode the reader has not chosen yet.\n  const row = recommendation.needsMode === true ? undefined : commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n  const command = recommendation.command ?? row?.command;\n  const owner = recommendation.ownerSkillId ?? row?.ownerSkillId ?? recommendation.skill;\n  const policy = recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy;\n  const commandPart = command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n  const ownerPart = sanitizeSkillLabel(owner);\n  if (!commandPart || !ownerPart) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  // The class belongs to the command printed, not to the skill that carried it,\n  // so a recommendation that names another command takes that command's class.\n  const mutating = row !== undefined && row.command === commandPart\n    ? row.mutating\n    : Object.values(COMMAND_ROWS).find((candidate) => candidate.command === commandPart)?.mutating;\n  const policyPart = policyWord(policy, mutating, childSession);\n  if (policyPart === null) {\n    return `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart}`;\n  }\n  // A typed command, with or without a mode suffix, is the reader's own choice,\n  // so the head prints it plainly instead of offering a choice already made.\n  return policyPart === 'ask' && DEEP_LOOP_OFFER_COMMANDS.has(commandPart) && recommendation.typed !== true\n    ? `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (ask: A ${commandPart}:auto (Recommended), B ${commandPart}:confirm, C no loop)`\n    : `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (${policyPart})`;\n}\n\n// A doctor bridge renders as its runnable command and never as its raw id; an\n// unmapped doctor id renders nothing.\nfunction recommendationLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  return commandLabel(recommendation, childSession)\n    ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(recommendation.skill)\n      ? doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill)\n      : sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill));\n}\n\n// A companion is a command the reader may act on, so it carries the same policy\n// word the head carries. A child still gets the downgrade marker because that\n// command must not be started there.\nfunction companionCommandLabel(skillId: string, childSession: boolean): string | null {\n  const command = doctorCommandString(skillId);\n  if (command === null) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  const row = commandRowFor(skillId);\n  const word = policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession);\n  return word === null ? command : `${command} (${word})`;\n}\n18:<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n24:| **Status** | Complete |\n94:| REQ-001 | The brief head for a `/deep:research` or `/deep:review` command with policy word `ask` names options A, B and C, with A the command plus `:auto` and B the command plus `:confirm`. | The Measured Behavior command prints `system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop)` in its first line, and the golden test for `/deep:research` expects the research names. |\n95:| REQ-002 | Every other command label renders as before. | `npx vitest run` in the advisor runtime reports 0 failed, and the golden heads for `/doctor:git hooks (ask)` and every non-deep row are unchanged in the diff. |\n96:| REQ-003 | A child session keeps the `parent-named only` label with no options. | A test renders a `/deep:review` recommendation with `childSession: true` and expects `(parent-named only)` with no `A ` option text. |\n102:| REQ-004 | The longer head still fits the default token cap with its companion line. | A test renders a `/deep:review` head with a `/doctor:deep-loop` companion at the default cap and expects both lines. |\n103:| REQ-005 | F6 is sampled four times after the change and the rate is recorded. | `implementation-summary.md` states how many of four F6 sessions asked the three-option offer, with each run's file under `scratch/behaviour/`. |\n104:| REQ-006 | A command the operator typed shows no offer options. For `/deep:review:confirm the auth module` and `/deep:research:auto vector index compaction` the brief prints `/deep:review (ask)` and `/deep:research (ask)` with no `A ` option text. | The prompt hook prints those heads, and a golden test pins each. |\n105:| REQ-007 | The tests pin the options to the deep-loop commands only. The head-length test accepts the colon form for `/deep:*` alone, and a golden test covers the offer in an ambiguous two-skill head. | Both tests fail when the options leak onto a non-deep `ask` command or drop out of the ambiguous head. |\n106:| REQ-008 | The packet says what was measured. `implementation-summary.md` states the eight-run result where it claimed sessions learn the options, quotes the final head, and records whether the Pi hand check ran. | `rg -n 'now learns' implementation-summary.md` prints nothing. |\n127:| Dependency | The behaviour arena from packet 012 (`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `claude -p` with a budget cap) | Without it SC-002 cannot be measured | Record REQ-005 as deferred with the reason and keep SC-001 as the closure evidence |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EGsZCPNgS33dqshPnJrDEP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
